        "original_id": "bc9b0473-15cf-5743-b534-4b47f5014c93",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Gatwick Airport, Heathrow Airport, Coldwaltham, Central London, Crawley, London, south-east England, United Kingdom\n- People: John Jocelyn Denison-Pender, 2nd Baron Pender\n- Codes: LGW, EGKK, LHR, EGLL\n- Topics: airport traffic ranking, travel distance\n\nFacts:\n- John Jocelyn Denison-Pender, 2nd Baron Pender, was born on 26 January 1907 and died on 21 March 1965.\n- John Jocelyn Denison-Pender, 2nd Baron Pender, was a British civil servant and businessman.\n- Gatwick Airport, also known as London Gatwick, is a major international airport in south-east England.\n- Gatwick Airport is 29.5 miles south of Central London and 2.7 nautical miles north of Crawley.\n- Gatwick Airport has the IATA code LGW and the ICAO code EGKK.\n- Gatwick Airport is the second-busiest airport in the United Kingdom by total passenger traffic after London Heathrow.\n- Heathrow Airport, also known as London Heathrow, is a major international airport in London, United Kingdom.\n- Heathrow Airport has the IATA code LHR and the ICAO code EGLL.\n- Coldwaltham is around a 30-minute drive from Gatwick Airport.",
